work_item=livespec-dev-tooling-z3wy33
reason=Change ONE branch of the incident-ci entrance step of .github/workflows/ci.yml: when the PR body carries a livespec-incident-ci block but the released plan selects a mode other than expedited-repair (an unlabeled PR, e.g. a factory repayment follow-up), the step prints a ::notice:: and a step-summary line and exits 0 before run/aggregate with `omitted` unwritten, instead of ::error:: + exit 1. That is the same no-op as the no-block path, required by z3wy33 assertion 4 ("an unexpedited factory follow-up pull request run[s] the complete normal policy with both incident flags forced off, regardless of any retained body block"). A plan refusal and a missing observer configuration stay red; no other job changes, the required-check set is unchanged, and CI runtime does not increase. Maintainer tier (two modified lines plus comments); approval recorded on the item.
